.TH CHTTPSVR_DESTROY 3 "2026-07-14" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_destroy \- destroy a chttpsvr handle and set it to CHTTPSVR_INVALID
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <chttpserver.h>

chttpsvr_destroy(name);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Calls __chttpsvr_destroy on name and then sets name to CHTTPSVR_INVALID.

__chttpsvr_destroy drains all in-flight requests, and if this is the
last active server also stops the shared engine.  Call chttpsvr_stop
first to close the listener before calling this macro.

Calling this a second time on an independently-held copy of the same
handle value (whether concurrently, or later, after the first call
has already completed), or calling it from within one of this
server's own request handlers/middleware, is a FATAL ERROR
(abort()/SIGABRT); see __chttpsvr_destroy(3).

Safe to call regardless of whether the shared engine is still running
(this releases name's own engine reference, possibly triggering an
asynchronous engine stop if it was the last one) or was already
force-stopped via chttpsvr_engine_stop() while name was still started;
see __chttpsvr_destroy's own documentation for why the latter case is
safe and idempotent.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR __chttpsvr_destroy (3),
.BR ___chttpsvr_destroy (3),
.BR chttpsvr_stop (3),
.BR chttpsvr_engine_stop (3),
.BR chttpsvr_engine_wait (3)
